    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d647">

                <pb facs="0769" n="763" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg763"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Executive Agreement Series No. 265</note>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6131/646a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador of the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Litvinov</hi>)<anchor n="95"
                        xml:id="d647-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-31">July 31, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In accordance with the
                    conversations which have taken place, I have the honor to confirm on behalf of
                    my Government the agreement which has been reached between the Governments of
                    our respective countries that the agreement regarding commercial relations
                    between the United States of America and the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics
                    recorded in the exchange of notes of August 4, 1937, which came into force on
                    August 6, 1937, and which was renewed on August 5, 1938,<anchor n="96"
                        xml:id="d647-f2"/> August 2, 1939,<anchor n="97" xml:id="d647-f3"/> August
                    6, 1940,<anchor n="98" xml:id="d647-f4"/> and August 2, 1941<anchor n="99"
                        xml:id="d647-f5"/> shall remain in force until August 6, 1943. It shall
                    continue in force thereafter, unless superseded by a more comprehensive
                    commercial, agreement, subject to termination on six months’ written notice by
                    either Government.</p>
                <p>The present agreement shall be proclaimed by the President of the United States
                    of America<anchor n="1" xml:id="d647-f6"/> and approved by the Council of
                    People’s Commissars of the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d647-f7"/>
                </p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cordell Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d647-f1" n="95" type="source" xml:id="d647-f1-content">
                <p>The same note, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, was sent at the
                    same time to the Secretary of State by the Soviet Ambassador (611.6131/647).
                    This exchange of notes constituted an agreement between the United States and
                    the Soviet Union, printed in Department of State Executive Agreement Series No.
                    265, and 56 Stat. (pt. 2) 1575. For text of press release issued by the
                    Department on July 31, 1942, see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, August 1, 1942, p. 662.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d647-f2" n="96" xml:id="d647-f2-content">
                <p>See <ref target="frus1933-39#pg_601">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, The Soviet Union, 1933–1939,
                        pp. 601</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d647-f3" n="97" xml:id="d647-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="frus1933-39#pg_809">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">ibid.</hi>, pp. 809</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d647-f4" n="98" xml:id="d647-f4-content">
                <p>See <ref target="frus1940v03#pg_441">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1940, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, pp. 441</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d647-f5" n="99" xml:id="d647-f5-content">
                <p>See <ref target="frus1941v01#pg_914">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, 1941, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >i</hi>, pp. 914</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d647-f6" n="1" xml:id="d647-f6-content">
                <p>This was done on August 1, 1942.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d647-f7" n="2" xml:id="d647-f7-content">
                <p>This approval was given on August 1, 1942.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
